  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A thin hafnium coating can improve the high-temperature oxidation resistance of zirconium-alloy nuclear-fuel cladding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::012::3_results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Refined sputtering or hot-press sintering parameters can produce the proposed optimized hafnium coating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A graded interlayer will promote formation of a coherent HfZr transition layer with the zirconium-alloy substrate.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded interlayer will promote controlled diffusion.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded interlayer and optimized process will minimize sintering shrinkage.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded interlayer and optimized process will reduce crack formation and delamination.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, zirconium diffuses from the substrate into the hafnium coating.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zirconium diffusion into the hafnium coating forms an HfZr alloy transition layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HfZr transition layer chemically bonds the hafnium coating to the substrate.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The graded interlayer mitigates thermal stresses and enhances coating-substrate bonding.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature oxidation of the hafnium coating produces a dense HfO2 film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::012::3_results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HfZr transition layer facilitates formation of the dense HfO2 film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10488483::web::012::3_results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dense HfO2 film protects the underlying material against deeper oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::012::3_results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to bare zirconium-alloy cladding, the coating will significantly reduce oxidation as measured by weight gain.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::012::3_results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to bare zirconium-alloy cladding, the coating will produce a thinner oxide layer.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coated cladding will retain appropriate mechanical performance for reactor service.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::000::abstract",
